 - 2026-06-16: PHASE C1 (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING -- the mandated self-learning experiment) -- re-power the online verifier-weight adaptation test on the LARGER family set. research-program.md mandates >=1 self-learning experiment/milestone; Tier 1 = online weight/counter updates (CPU, <1us/update, NOT the retired live-LoRA path). .395 found static-is-the-ceiling BUT the (online-static) CI only TOUCHED 0 at n=52 ([0.0, 0.192]) -- an n-limit, not a proven null. RE-RUN the Tier-1 online reweighting across the COMBINED family set (the .395 recovered manifest + ARC-GEN's many families from exp4282, a soft input) so the CI is POWERED, AND add a Tier-2 constraint-memory arm (cache per-family selection patterns, reuse on the nearest-neighbor seen family) as a distinct mechanism. Report static vs online vs Tier-2 cross-family delta + the per-family adaptation curve + a POWERED CI95 on (online-static). Emit online_adaptation_helps BARE bool := (online-static>0 AND CI95-excl-0). A positive gain = the verifier self-improves toward generalization (north-star-grade); a null WITH POWER = static is genuinely the ceiling (retire the online-adaptation-helps ask). verifier_is_oracle=false. NO fine-tuning; NO TRM; NO live-LoRA. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: powered_static_is_the_ceiling_for_self_learning; results/experiment_4283_self_learning_repowered_arcgen.json
 - 2026-06-16: PHASE D1 (the owed north-star §5 EFFICIENCY axis) -- energy-verifier vs LLM-as-judge head-to-head on the ORACLE-DISTINCT cross-family ARC selection. north-star §5 names the verifier's win condition: 'equally effective as the LM at lower cost/latency' (efficiency-parity), and names this head-to-head as load-bearing-owed work. On the SAME held-out-family cross-family selection task (the oracle-distinct domain -- NOT code, whose efficiency-vs-judge is retired/circular), compare the learned energy verifier's selection accuracy vs an LLM-as-judge (a cached SOTA GGUF -- Qwen3.6-35B-A3B or gemma-4 -- selecting from the same candidates). Report accuracy parity (within CI) AND the compute/latency/cost ratio (wall-clock, FLOPs-proxy, $/1k selections). Emit efficiency_parity_at_lower_cost BARE bool := (energy-verifier accuracy within the LLM-judge CI AND energy-verifier cost <= 0.1x the LLM-judge cost). Target: 'parity at 10-100x cheaper' (CompassVerifier 2508.03686 / Luna-2 small-verifier precedent: 60-1000x). verifier_is_oracle=false. This is a NEW measurement (the §5 owed axis), NOT a re-run. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: efficiency_parity_at_lower_cost_true_delta_0.4423; results/experiment_4284_verifier_efficiency_vs_llm_judge.json
